[{'canonical_issue_id': 16, 'id': 16, 'name': 'accessibility', 'description': 'The interface creates barriers for users with accessibility needs by lacking proper assistive technology support, keyboard usability, visual contrast, non-color cues, or adequately sized interactive targets. These issues can make content, controls, status, or actions difficult to perceive, understand, navigate, or operate.', 'aliases': ['screen reader issue', 'missing ARIA', 'unlabeled control', 'inaccessible markup', 'keyboard trap', 'poor tab order', 'missing focus', 'keyboard inaccessible', 'low contrast', 'inaccessible colors', 'weak visibility', 'color contrast issue', 'color dependency', 'color-only status', 'inaccessible state', 'no non-color cue', 'tiny button', 'hard to tap', 'small hit area', 'cramped controls'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'The screen reader announced the button as button but did not say what it did. I tabbed through the page but could not reach the dropdown menu. The gray text on the white background was almost impossible to read. The only difference between available and unavailable dates was the color. I kept tapping the wrong icon because the buttons were too close together.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 687797, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 687805, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 1, 'id': 1, 'name': 'bug', 'description': 'Functional problems where the interface or feature behaves incorrectly, fails, crashes, breaks, or produces unexpected results.', 'aliases': ['bug', 'bugs', 'error', 'errors', 'crash', 'crashed', 'crashes', 'broken', 'breaks', 'glitch', 'glitched', 'failed', 'failure', "doesn't work", 'did not work', 'not working', 'stopped working', 'unexpected', 'wrong', 'issue', 'problem'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'The app crashed when I opened the workout summary. The reminder settings did not work after I saved them. I got an uknown error when trying to update my profile. The streak screen showed the wrong number of days. The search feature stopped working during the session.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 676996, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 677011, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 2, 'id': 2, 'name': 'confusion', 'description': 'Situations where users do not understand what the interface means, what they should do next, or how to interpret the available options.', 'aliases': ['confusing', 'confused', 'unclear', 'ambiguous', 'lost', "didn't understand", 'did not understand', "don't understand", 'not sure', 'unsure', 'uncertain', "couldn't figure out", 'could not figure out', 'hard to understand', 'where to', 'what to do', 'how to', 'no idea', 'blended together', 'ambiguity', 'unclear field', 'format confusion', 'input ambiguity', 'hidden interaction', 'misleading'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'I was confused by the labels on the workout screen. I did not understand what to do after finishing the routine. The settings options were unclear and blended together. I was not sure how to change the reminder time. I could not figure out where to see my streak progress. The phone number field failed, but it never showed the required format. The heading looked like a button, but clicking it did nothing. I did not know whether the icon meant share, upload, or send. I thought I was editing the live page, but I was only changing a draft.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 678513, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 678532, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 8, 'id': 8, 'name': 'content quality', 'description': 'Content quality problems where information is incorrect, outdated, missing, excessive, irrelevant, misleading, or poorly explained.', 'aliases': ['wrong information', 'incorrect', 'outdated', 'missing information', 'not enough information', 'too much information', 'misleading', 'irrelevant', 'not relevant', 'poor explanation'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'The workout explanation had missing information. The progress screen showed incorrect details. The reminder instructions were unclear. The help text gave too much information for a simple setting. The streak description felt misleading.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 683058, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 683069, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 15, 'id': 15, 'name': 'high cognitive load', 'description': 'The interface presents too much information, too many decisions, or too many competing elements at once. Users must work harder than necessary to understand what matters and what to do next.', 'aliases': ['mental overload', 'clutter', 'too many options', 'high effort', 'long form', 'form friction', 'excessive fields', 'tedious input', 'tedious', 'overwhelmed', 'analysis paralysis', 'headache'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'The screen had too many options, and I did not know where to start. The form felt tedious because there were too many fields to fill out. There was so much clutter that I missed the button I needed. I felt overwhelmed because everything was shown at once.The app made a simple task feel like high effort. There were so many settings on the page that I did not know where to start.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 687240, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 687248, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 17, 'id': 17, 'name': 'inefficient workflow', 'description': 'The interface makes users complete tasks with more effort than necessary. Workflows may include too many steps, unnecessary fields, repeated information, poor defaults, excessive confirmations, broken paths, hidden features, scattered comparison details, or unclear choices. Users can often finish the task, but the process feels slower, harder, or more cumbersome than it should.', 'aliases': ['too many steps', 'inefficient flow', 'excessive clicks', 'slow workflow', 'too many prompts', 'modal fatigue', 'unnecessary confirmation', 'interruptive dialog', 'dead link', 'broken path', 'navigation dead end', 'missing destination', 'hidden feature', 'low discoverability', 'hard to find', 'feature invisibility', 'hard comparison', 'comparison friction', 'option confusion', 'decision support issue', 'too many choices', 'choice overload', 'unclear decision', 'option overload'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'I had to enter the same address twice during checkout. To update one setting, I had to go through four different screens. It asked me to confirm every small change, which slowed me down. The Help link opened a 404 page. I did not realize there was a bulk edit option until someone showed me. I had to open each plan in a separate tab to compare the features. There were five subscription options and I could not tell which one I needed.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 688373, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 688381, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 4, 'id': 4, 'name': 'interaction friction', 'description': 'Interaction difficulties where using the interface feels harder, more tedious, more awkward, or more frustrating than users expect.', 'aliases': ['hard', 'difficult', 'awkward', 'annoying', 'frustrating', 'frustration', 'tedious', 'cumbersome', 'clunky', 'painful', 'too many steps', 'too much work', 'hard to use', 'difficult to use', 'not intuitive', 'counterintuitive', 'inconvenient', 'settings friction', 'poor preferences', 'limited control', 'customization issue', 'interruptive modal', 'annoying popup', 'intrusive prompt', 'flow interruption', 'bad button placement', 'misplaced action', 'detached control', 'action confusion', 'timeout issue', 'unexpected logout', 'expired session', 'session loss', 'frustrating experience', 'low satisfaction', 'emotional friction', 'unpleasant UX'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'It was hard to use the app while setting up my routine. Changing the reminder was annoying because it took too many steps. The workout setup felt clunky and inconvenient. The process was frustrating when I only wanted to start quickly. The flow was not intuitive for a simple cardio day. I wanted fewer notifications but could not find the setting. A newsletter popup covered the form before I could finish reading it. I clicked Delete thinking it applied to one item, but it deleted the whole group. I was logged out while writing the form and lost everything. I completed the task, but the process felt annoying and stressful.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 679762, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 679772, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 5, 'id': 5, 'name': 'navigation friction', 'description': 'Wayfinding problems where users struggle to locate screens, controls, settings, content, or paths through the interface.', 'aliases': ["couldn't find", 'could not find', "can't find", 'cannot find', 'hard to find', 'where is', 'where are', 'menu', 'navigation', 'navigate', 'back', 'next', 'search', 'filter', 'hidden', 'buried', 'missing', 'not visible', 'menu labels', 'dropdown menu', 'confusing navigation', 'poor wayfinding', 'hidden routes', 'unclear menu', 'buried CTA', 'invisible action', 'hard-to-find button', 'weak primary action'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': "I couldn't find the reminder settings. The streak screen was hard to find. I was not sure where the settings menu was. The filter option seemed hidden from the main screen. I had trouble navigating back to the routine page. I could not find where to change my account settings. I wanted to submit the form, but the button was hidden at the bottom.", 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 680395, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 680405, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 3, 'id': 3, 'name': 'performance', 'description': 'Speed and responsiveness problems where the interface is slow, delayed, laggy, frozen, stuck, or otherwise unresponsive.', 'aliases': ['slow', 'slower', 'lag', 'laggy', 'lagging', 'delay', 'delayed', 'loading', 'took too long', 'takes too long', 'waited', 'freeze', 'freezes', 'frozen', 'stuck', 'hang', 'hanging', 'unresponsive', 'timeout', 'timed out', 'slow performance', 'long loading'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'The app was slow when loading the workout history. The streak screen took too long to appear. The routine froze halfway through the session. I waited for the reminder settings page to load. The app felt laggy when switching between screens. The refund policy was under Help, but I expected it under Orders. I was not sure whether Continue would save my changes or skip the step. The form defaulted to public visibility, but I expected private. I did not know what provisioning a workspace meant. I had to read every paragraph to find the delivery date. The dashboard showed a score but did not explain whether it was good or bad. The date 06/11 was ambiguous and I was not sure which month it meant.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 679161, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 679170, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 18, 'id': 18, 'name': 'permissions', 'description': 'Users cannot understand why they can or cannot access something, what permission is needed, or how to request access. The system may block users without explanation.', 'aliases': ['access issue', 'permission confusion', 'blocked action', 'role confusion'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'The button was disabled, but it did not say what permission I needed. I tried to open the page, but it just said I did not have permission. The app blocked the action without explaining why. I could not tell what access I needed to continue. The screen said I was not allowed, but it did not tell me how to request access. I was confused because another user could see the option, but I could not.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 688941, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 688951, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 12, 'id': 12, 'name': 'poor error recovery', 'description': 'After an error occurs, users have difficulty correcting it or returning to a safe state. They may lose entered data, be forced to restart, or receive no path to resolve the problem.', 'aliases': ['hard recovery', 'lost progress', 'restart required', 'had to restart', 'lost my save', "couldn't recover", 'did not recover', 'stuck', 'got stuck', 'dead end error', 'lost data', 'cleared form', 'reset input', 'surprising behavior', 'unexpected change', 'sudden reset', 'unpredictable state', 'no undo', 'irreversible action', 'poor recovery', 'restore issue'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'I got stuck and had to restart the whole thing.\nI got stuck and had to restart the whole thing. The app crashed and I lost my progress. I made a mistake, but there was no way to go back. After the error, I could not recover what I had entered. The screen became a dead end, so I had to start over.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 685572, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 685580, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 11, 'id': 11, 'name': 'poor error validation', 'description': 'The interface does not adequately prevent avoidable user mistakes before they happen, allowing errors through weak validation, dangerous defaults, confusing controls, or missing constraints.', 'aliases': ['avoidable error', 'weak validation', 'unsafe default', 'preventable mistake', 'error traps', 'avoidable mistakes', 'preventable errors', 'missing validation', 'dangerous defaults', 'confusing controls', 'missing constraints', 'accidental errors', 'error-prone controls', 'vague error', 'technical error', 'unclear failure', 'bad error copy'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': "The form was missing validation on the required fields. I choose the wrong option without realizing it. I got an unexpected error during checkout. The app let me submit forms with empty mandatory fields. The form didn't tell me what errors I made and it didn't let me save. I couldn't understand the error messages. The error messages were cryptic and ambiguous.", 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 685013, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 685021, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 10, 'id': 10, 'name': 'poor feedback', 'description': 'The system does not clearly confirm that an action has been received, completed, failed, or is still processing. Users are left uncertain about the state of the system.', 'aliases': ['no feedback', 'silent action', 'missing confirmation', 'unclear response', 'unclear status', 'missing state', 'no progress indicator', 'state confusion', 'no progress', 'unclear steps', 'missing stepper', 'process uncertainty', 'dangerous action', 'weak warning', 'accidental deletion', 'destructive action issue', 'too many alerts', 'notification fatigue', 'noisy notifications', 'irrelevant alerts', 'empty screen', 'dead end', 'no results guidance', 'blank state', 'no results issue', 'empty results', 'search dead end', 'filter dead end'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': "The button did nothing when I tapped it. I submitted the form but got no confirmation. The app was loading, but I could not tell if it was still working. I saved my changes, but nothing told me they were saved. The screen gave no response after I clicked continue. After I hit save, there was no confirmation message. I can't tell if the app is still running or if it is stuck.", 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 684429, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 684437, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 9, 'id': 9, 'name': 'poor learnability', 'description': 'The interface behaves differently across similar pages, components, or workflows. Users must relearn interactions because buttons, menus, icons, gestures, or layouts do not work consistently. Controls, flows, terminology, and system behavior do not teach themselves clearly through design.', 'aliases': ['hard to learn', 'steep learning curve', 'confusing first use', 'unintuitive UI', 'inconsistent UI', 'unpredictable behavior', 'pattern mismatch', 'interaction inconsistency', 'weak onboarding', 'poor first-time use', 'lack of guidance', 'confusing start', 'weak help', 'poor documentation', 'missing guidance', 'unhelpful support'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': "The app was hard to learn because the main actions were not obvious at first. The interface had a steep learning curve, especially during the first setup. The interface did not make sense and I couldn't remember how to do things. The same button had different uses in different pages. The interface was inconsistent. The buttons, links, and calls to action made the app feel unintuitive.", 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 683825, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 683836, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 14, 'id': 14, 'name': 'poor memorability', 'description': 'Users who return after time away cannot easily remember how to perform tasks. The interface depends too much on recall instead of recognition, or uses inconsistent paths and labels.', 'aliases': ['hard to remember', 'recall burden', 'forgettable workflow', 'low recognizability', "didn't remember", "couldn't remember", "can't recall", 'forgot where', 'forgot how', 'had to relearn', 'needed to relearn', 'not memorable', 'hard to find again', 'where was it', 'lost track', 'could not remember', 'forgot the steps', 'had to figure it out again', 'not familiar anymore'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'I used this last week but could not remember where the export option was. I used this before, but I forgot where the option was. I came back later and had to figure it out again. I could not remember the steps to finish the task. The feature was hard to find again after a few days. I had to relearn how to do something I already did last week.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 686683, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 686691, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 19, 'id': 19, 'name': 'poor mobile responsiveness', 'description': 'The interface does not adapt well to smaller screens. Content may overflow, controls may become cramped, important actions may disappear, or layouts may require excessive scrolling.', 'aliases': ['bad mobile layout', 'responsive issue', 'mobile friction', 'broken small screen', "doesn't fit screen", 'content overflow', 'cut off on mobile', 'cramped layout', 'tiny controls', 'too much scrolling', 'horizontal scrolling', 'mobile view broken', 'button disappeared', 'hard to use on phone', 'poor phone layout', 'small screen issue', 'layout breaks', 'not mobile friendly', 'mobile usability issue', 'page does not scale'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'On my phone, the table was cut off and I could not see the action buttons. The page did not fit my phone screen. The buttons were too cramped on mobile. I had to scroll sideways to see the full content. The layout broke when I opened it on my phone. An important button disappeared on the small screen.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 689456, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 689465, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 6, 'id': 6, 'name': 'poor readability', 'description': 'Readability problems that make the interface difficult to perceive, read, navigate, or operate for users with different needs or contexts.', 'aliases': ['hard to read', 'small text', 'too small', 'illegible', "can't read", 'cannot read', 'dificult to read', 'poor legibility', 'contrast', "can't see", 'cannot see', 'difficult to see', 'color', 'screen reader', 'keyboard', 'tab', 'focus', 'accessible', 'accessibility', 'disabled', 'vision', 'hearing', 'trouble reading', 'dense text', 'text overload'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'The text was too small to read comfortably. The contrast made the progress screen difficult to see. I had trouble reading the workout instructions. The focus state was hard to notice when using the keyboard. The color choices made the reminder screen less readable.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 680967, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 680976, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 20, 'id': 20, 'name': 'privacy concern', 'description': 'Users cannot understand or confidently manage what information is shared, visible, stored, tracked, or used. Privacy settings may be hidden, vague, or overly complex.', 'aliases': ['privacy friction', 'unclear visibility', 'data control issue', 'sharing confusion', 'privacy settings', 'hidden privacy settings', 'unclear privacy settings', 'data sharing', 'shared without knowing', 'who can see this', 'visibility settings', 'tracking concern', 'data tracking', 'stored data', 'data use', 'personal data', 'privacy confusion', 'hard to manage privacy', 'public by default', 'private information'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'I could not tell who would be able to see my profile information. I could not tell who could see my information. The privacy settings were hard to find. I was not sure what data the app was storing. The app did not explain what information was being shared. I wanted to change my visibility, but the setting was unclear.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 689948, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 689955, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 21, 'id': 21, 'name': 'redundancy', 'description': 'Users are asked to repeat actions, confirmations, entries, selections, or decisions that the system should remember or infer. This creates unnecessary friction and frustration.', 'aliases': ['repetition', 'duplicate effort', 'repeated input', 'redundant step', 'had to enter again', 'asked again', 'same information twice', 'repeat action', 'repeat confirmation', 'duplicate step', 'unnecessary repeat', 're-enter information', 'kept asking', 'already answered', 'already selected', 'did not remember my choice', 'unnecessary confirmation', 'extra confirmation', 'same question again', 'manual repetition'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'Every time I opened the page, I had to select the same preferences again. The app asked me to enter the same information twice. I had to choose the same option again on the next screen. The system did not remember what I had already selected. I had to confirm the same thing more than once. The process felt repetitive because I kept doing the same step again.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 690461, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 690468, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 22, 'id': 22, 'name': 'search quality', 'description': 'Search, filtering, or sorting does not help users find the right results efficiently. Results may be irrelevant, poorly ranked, hard to narrow down, or empty without useful suggestions, and users may struggle to apply, combine, reset, or understand filters and sorting options.', 'aliases': ['bad search', 'irrelevant results', 'weak filtering', 'search friction', 'filter friction', 'sorting issue', 'hidden filters', 'unclear results', 'poor ranking', 'wrong results', 'no results', 'empty results', 'bad results', 'hard to filter', 'filters did not work', 'filter confusion', 'active filter unclear', 'could not narrow results', 'hard to sort', 'sort did not work', 'results changed unexpectedly', 'missing filters', 'too many results', 'search did not help', 'could not find result'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'The search gave me results that did not match what I typed. I could not narrow the results because the filters were hard to use. The app showed no results but did not suggest anything else. I could not tell if a filter was still active. The sorting changed the results, but I did not understand why.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 690943, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 690949, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 7, 'id': 7, 'name': 'trust', 'description': 'Trust and confidence problems where users feel concerned, suspicious, unsafe, hesitant, or unsure whether the interface is reliable or secure.', 'aliases': ["don't trust", 'do not trust', 'not trustworthy', 'suspicious', 'unsafe', 'privacy', 'security', 'scam', 'fake', 'unreliable', 'concerned', 'worried', 'hesitant', 'not confident'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'I was worried about the privacy settings. The app felt unreliable after showing inconsistent progress. I was hesitant to share personal fitness data. The security message made me feel concerned. I was not confident that my reminder changes were saved. The payment page looked different from the rest of the site, so I hesitated.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 682215, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 682233, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}, {'canonical_issue_id': 13, 'id': 13, 'name': 'visual clutter', 'description': 'The screen is visually overloaded or poorly prioritized, making it hard for users to scan, understand what matters, and decide what to do next. Dense content, crowded spacing, competing colors, excessive decoration, weak emphasis, or unclear priority can make important information and actions harder to notice.', 'aliases': ['busy layout', 'cluttered screen', 'crowded UI', 'noisy design', 'weak hierarchy', 'poor emphasis', 'unclear priority', 'flat layout', 'visual overload', 'too much on screen', 'hard to scan', 'dense content', 'crowded layout', 'messy screen', 'competing colors', 'poor spacing', 'unclear layout', 'important things hidden', 'everything looks the same', 'too many elements'], 'source': 'EVALUATOR', 'examples': 'The screen felt too busy, and I did not know where to look first. There was too much on the page, so I missed the main button. Everything looked equally important, which made the page hard to scan. The layout felt crowded and messy. The important information did not stand out.', 'status': 'APPROVED', 'is_active': True, 'created_by': 2, 'created_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 686127, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), 'updated_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 6, 28, 12, 3, 6, 686135, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)}]